    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point: exploiting the matchup against Jake Bennett. The primary beneficiary is **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40), who stands as our strongest play of the day. The combination of a favorable platoon edge, park factors, and Bennett\u2019s deliberate pace\u2014which historically inflates stolen base opportunities\u2014propels **Luis Robert Jr.** into elite territory. We are also leaning heavily on the left-handed bats of **Coby Mayo** (62.75) and **Gunnar Henderson** (65.12) against Bennett; while the platoon metrics for **Gunnar Henderson** show a slight regression, the 16% boost from the park factor and the potential for aggressive base running against a slow-working starter make him a high-floor cornerstone for our lineup.\n\nRounding out the core, **Kyle Tucker** (65.64) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.99) provide reliable production despite facing tough arms in Quinn Mathews and Tanner Bibee, respectively. **Sam Antonacci** (61.20) benefits significantly from his leadoff spot, providing the requisite efficiency we demand at second base. While **Liam Hicks** (52.44) and **Miguel Vargas** (52.92) sit in the marginal tier, they remain locked into the starting lineup due to a lack of viable alternatives on the bench. We continue to monitor the status of **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg**; with **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined on the IL, our depth is thin, forcing us to lean on the current active roster to maintain our daily game cap efficiency.\n\nThe most notable tactical decision today involved the bottom of the order, where the margin between **Liam Hicks** and potential bench depth remains razor-thin. While **Liam Hicks** carries a pedestrian projection, the lack of availability from **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose team is off today, leaves us without a viable plug-and-play upgrade. We are proceeding with caution regarding the lineups for **Liam Hicks**, **Coby Mayo**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**; as these are currently pending, any shift in the batting order\u2014specifically if **Gunnar Henderson** or **Luis Robert Jr.** drops out of the top four\u2014could necessitate a recalibration of our expected output for the afternoon.",
